Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 02:40:40 +0000

In "Re: [RFC] re-thinking SMTP relay" [1] Pat asked that the tool which
delivers mail to the list accept only a correctly formatted message.
Under that design git send-email hands each message to
maildir-deliver.sh as its sendmail program, so this series puts the
check there. It refuses input whose headers are malformed or not
ended by an empty line, or that lacks exactly one From, Subject, and
Message-ID, and writes nothing to the maildir when it does.

The first patch makes the patch-triage skill compose a From and a
Message-ID, which it left out, so that skill keeps working once the
check is in.

Tested with the new atf tests (kyua test in libexec/mail), which fail
against the current script, and by delivering 30 messages from the
list and a git format-patch series into a scratch maildir; all were
accepted.

